#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087460 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6381faa4-5dfd-58fa-ace7-411fd2a97e98" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the x-Intercepts of an Ellipse By Completing the Square"}] :question/id #uuid "58d92951-d993-50ec-806c-802c627ada96" :question/math-academy-id "e-5213" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse $x^2 + 3y^2 - 4x - 6y = 2$ (shown above) intercepts the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/850/Source/Images/7a5d03c5fc0581217a488b76e6d39486.png)" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y = 0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x$. We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + 3y^{2} - 4x - 6y &= 2 \\\\\nx^{2} + 3 \\cdot 0^{2} - 4x - 6 \\cdot 0 &= 2 \\\\\nx^{2} - 4x &= 2 \\\\\n(x^{2} - 4x + 4) - 4 &= 2 \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} - 4 &= 2 \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} &= 6 \\\\\nx - 2 &= ± \\sqrt{6} \\\\\nx &= 2 ± \\sqrt{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(2-\\sqrt{6},0)$ and $(2+\\sqrt{6},0)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087461 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a508c1-2379-590f-85f5-386a1990f137" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the x-Intercepts of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "a7fe6697-669c-57e2-8415-4bd40cf76dac" :question/math-academy-id "e-5214" :question/problem "Calculate the point where the ellipse $(x-2)^2 + \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{4} = 1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y = 0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x$. Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 2)^{2} + ((y - 2)^{2})/(4) &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + ((0 - 2)^{2})/(4) &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + 1 &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx - 2 &= 0 \\\\\nx &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the point $(2,0)$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/850/Source/Images/c435c838bf3a88b169499c58834c75c4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a57ec9ff-99fd-5a3d-9a89-e76ded9d01cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the y-Intercepts of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "85e115e3-4f55-53e6-9d3b-decb3dc02267" :question/math-academy-id "e-5220" :question/problem "Calculate the point where the ellipse $\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{4}+\\dfrac{(y-3)^2}{16}=1$ intercepts the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x = 0$ in the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $y$. Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((x - 1)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 3)^{2})/(16) &= 1 \\\\\n((0 - 1)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 3)^{2})/(16) &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{1}{4} + ((y - 3)^{2})/(16) &= 1 \\\\\n((y - 3)^{2})/(16) &= \\frac{3}{4} \\\\\n(y - 3)^{2} &= 12 \\\\\ny - 3 &= ± \\sqrt{12} \\\\\ny - 3 &= 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\\ny &= 3 ± 2\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the points $(0,3 -2\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,3 +2\\sqrt{3})$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/850/Source/Images/686d5b60b8ea3f16af57af3ed5ef341d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fea426db-a854-5efc-a0cd-7d52019a7cc6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the y-Intercepts of an Ellipse By Completing the Square"}] :question/id #uuid "5cbcffa6-eb3d-5438-ba08-4b47cbbf76ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-5221" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse $5x^2 + 2y^2 - 20x - 8y + 13 = 0$ intercepts the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $y$-intercepts, we need to substitute $x = 0$ in the equation of the ellipse and try to solve the resulting equation for $y$. We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x^{2} + 2y^{2} - 20x - 8y + 13 &= 0 \\\\\n5 \\cdot 0^{2} + 2y^{2} - 20 \\cdot 0 - 8y + 13 &= 0 \\\\\n2y^{2} - 8y + 13 &= 0 \\\\\n2(y^{2} - 4y) + 13 &= 0 \\\\\n2[y^{2} - 4y + 4 - 4] + 13 &= 0 \\\\\n2[(y - 2)^{2} - 4] + 13 &= 0 \\\\\n2(y - 2)^{2} + 5 &= 0 \\\\\n(y - 2)^{2} &= -\\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n(y-2)^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\n, there is no $y$ such that\n\n$$\n(y-2)^2 = -\\dfrac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse has no $y$-intercepts, meaning that it does not intercept the $y$-axis at any point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/850/Source/Images/dadec72b5f61bde4c28bdf1079eb4729.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a57ec9ff-99fd-5a3d-9a89-e76ded9d01cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the y-Intercepts of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f0d9c56-8bc0-59bb-aaaa-ba7b2d977ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0, 4.5)$ and $(0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084922} {:answer/id #uuid "b95182a8-65ec-5089-832d-a4feab67c09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 4.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084923} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9d5abd-983f-55c1-80f1-68f0a0e45f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 1.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084924} {:answer/id #uuid "5325a49f-8386-539a-9551-50271273c3e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0, 1.5)$ and $(0, 4.5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084925} {:answer/id #uuid "6b504e5c-db51-5203-aabf-1e5b16a33fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no $y$-intercept" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b504e5c-db51-5203-aabf-1e5b16a33fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no $y$-intercept" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084926} :answer-field/id #uuid "3be5e4f8-3f21-5664-af45-90a5f44162d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084921}] :question/id #uuid "93774ab1-c034-5d25-91bb-1dbd3d1f509d" :question/math-academy-id "q-16682" :question/problem "Determine the points where the ellipse $((x - 3)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 2)^{2})/(9) = 1$ intercepts the $y$-axis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a508c1-2379-590f-85f5-386a1990f137" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the x-Intercepts of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cb3c0df-3832-577b-827a-26d8e4d65bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5, 0)$ and $(-3, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087319} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a6f6ab-b141-5abe-bc31-f1709de323bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(3, 0)$ and $(5, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087320} {:answer/id #uuid "0481e7c3-6950-5fe0-8d3d-2ea93680d586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4, 0)$ and $(-2, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087321} {:answer/id #uuid "398d82c9-4cc1-547d-9f52-d8b2e613f1ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2, 0)$ and $(2, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087322} {:answer/id #uuid "53af3dde-ce2b-5aee-a79c-d7d102c042de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2, 0)$ and $(4, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cb3c0df-3832-577b-827a-26d8e4d65bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5, 0)$ and $(-3, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087319} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d6b1db7-08c4-56d0-a6bb-ce1468649e28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087318}] :question/id #uuid "8fc78834-5b61-5384-b707-af7562e6a703" :question/math-academy-id "q-9457" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse $((x + 4)^{2})/(3) + ((y + 2)^{2})/(6) = 1$ intercepts the $x$-axis."}]}
